  "findings": [
    "The fixed .75 log-odds shift improves partial-label body IoU from 79.85% to 83.66%, but reduces crop proposals from 3/22 to 2/22. No new proposal is recovered.",
    "The lost foliage-background checker retains adequate lobe support (0.833,0.806) and low cap-colour loss (0.056,0.004), but right lower-edge support drops from 0.653 to 0.623, below the unchanged 0.65 threshold. The failure is therefore not a soft cap-confidence veto.",
    "The two retained proposals move: partial known-region body IoU drops slightly for the candle and improves slightly for the blue/yellow checker. Both changed proposals and the lost checker were visually inspected.",
    "Background clutter remains visible in the adjusted masks. A single global operating-point shift does not reproduce the benefits of correcting known background pixels.",
    "This rejects the tested operating point only; it does not prove that every calibration method or threshold fails. No full template fitting is justified by these crop outcomes."
  ],
